  "title": "#AskNASA┃Is the Sun a ball of fire?",
  "description": "Is the Sun a ball of fire? And why does NASA send missions to the Sun? NASA’s Heliophysics Director Nicky Fox explains NASA’s latest solar science findings. The Parker Solar Probe mission is revolutionizing our understanding of the Sun, where changing conditions can propagate out into the solar system, affecting Earth and other worlds. It will travel through the Sun’s atmosphere, closer to the surface than any spacecraft before it, facing brutal heat and radiation conditions — and ultimately providing humanity with the closest-ever observations of a star.",
  "keywords": "Nicky Fox, Sun, Heliophysics, Parker Solar Probe, Fox, Parker",
  "date": "2020-01-06T00:00:00Z",
  "branch": "NASA",
  "unit_name": "NASA",
  "credit": "NASA video",
  "page_url": "https://images.nasa.gov/details/NHQ_2020_0106_AskNASA",
  "via": "the NASA Image and Video Library",
  "license": "Public domain (NASA work, U.S. government)",
  "location": {},
  "time_start": 0.0,
  "id": "nasa-NHQ-2020-0106-AskNASA",
  "status": "new",
  "harvested_at": "2026-11-12T00:47:16Z",
  "duration": 335.02,
  "source_file": {
    "src": "https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/NHQ_2020_0106_AskNASA/NHQ_2020_0106_AskNASA~orig.mp4",
    "width": 1920,
    "height": 1080,
    "duration": 335.001333
  },
  "transcript_source": "captions",
  "transcript": [
    {
      "s": 0.33,
      "e": 1.74,
      "text": ">> Hi, I'm Nicky Fox."
    },
    {
      "s": 1.8,
      "e": 2.87,
      "text": "And I'm in charge of all"
    },
    {
      "s": 2.94,
      "e": 4.84,
      "text": "sun science here at NASA."
    },
    {
      "s": 4.9,
      "e": 6.21,
      "text": "Oh."
    },
    {
      "s": 6.27,
      "e": 7.67,
      "text": "This is \"Ask NASA,\""
    },
    {
      "s": 7.74,
      "e": 8.61,
      "text": "and I'm here to answer"
    },
    {
      "s": 8.68,
      "e": 9.88,
      "text": "your questions."
    },
    {
      "s": 16.15,
      "e": 18.45,
      "text": "\"Is the sun a ball of fire?\""
    },
    {
      "s": 18.52,
      "e": 21.52,
      "text": "No, it's not."
    },
    {
      "s": 21.59,
      "e": 22.66,
      "text": "We know that the sun"
    },
    {
      "s": 22.72,
      "e": 24.02,
      "text": "can't be a ball of fire,"
    },
    {
      "s": 24.09,
      "e": 25.09,
      "text": "because we need oxygen"
    },
    {
      "s": 25.16,
      "e": 26.76,
      "text": "to be able to have combustion"
    },
    {
      "s": 26.83,
      "e": 29.16,
      "text": "and there's no oxygen in space."
    },
    {
      "s": 29.23,
      "e": 30.43,
      "text": "The sun, however,"
    },
    {
      "s": 30.5,
      "e": 33.0,
      "text": "is a giant nuclear furnace."
    },
    {
      "s": 33.07,
      "e": 34.77,
      "text": "The core in the very center"
    },
    {
      "s": 34.83,
      "e": 36.1,
      "text": "is very, very similar"
    },
    {
      "s": 36.17,
      "e": 37.47,
      "text": "to a nuclear reactor."
    },
    {
      "s": 37.54,
      "e": 38.47,
      "text": "And all of the--"
    },
    {
      "s": 38.54,
      "e": 39.34,
      "text": "these particles get"
    },
    {
      "s": 39.41,
      "e": 40.97,
      "text": "squashed together and there's"
    },
    {
      "s": 41.04,
      "e": 42.64,
      "text": "a huge amount of pressure."
    },
    {
      "s": 42.71,
      "e": 44.01,
      "text": "And they go--"
    },
    {
      "s": 44.08,
      "e": 45.84,
      "text": "undergo chemical reactions."
    },
    {
      "s": 45.91,
      "e": 47.18,
      "text": "And so there are very different"
    },
    {
      "s": 47.25,
      "e": 49.42,
      "text": "layers as you move out"
    },
    {
      "s": 49.48,
      "e": 51.42,
      "text": "towards the edge of the sun."
    },
    {
      "s": 51.48,
      "e": 53.22,
      "text": "\"Why does NASA send"
    },
    {
      "s": 53.29,
      "e": 55.35,
      "text": "missions to the sun?\""
    },
    {
      "s": 55.42,
      "e": 56.09,
      "text": "Because the sun"
    },
    {
      "s": 56.16,
      "e": 57.72,
      "text": "is the most important thing"
    },
    {
      "s": 57.79,
      "e": 59.39,
      "text": "in our solar system."
    },
    {
      "s": 59.46,
      "e": 61.39,
      "text": "The sun generates light"
    },
    {
      "s": 61.46,
      "e": 62.4,
      "text": "but also a tremendous"
    },
    {
      "s": 62.46,
      "e": 63.73,
      "text": "amount of energy."
    },
    {
      "s": 63.8,
      "e": 65.06,
      "text": "And it sends all of this"
    },
    {
      "s": 65.13,
      "e": 67.77,
      "text": "material to us here on Earth,"
    },
    {
      "s": 67.83,
      "e": 69.5,
      "text": "and so we live in the extended"
    },
    {
      "s": 69.57,
      "e": 71.3,
      "text": "atmosphere of the sun."
    },
    {
      "s": 71.37,
      "e": 72.41,
      "text": "We've looked at the sun"
    },
    {
      "s": 72.47,
      "e": 74.14,
      "text": "in every different wavelength."
    },
    {
      "s": 74.21,
      "e": 76.11,
      "text": "But recently, NASA launched"
    },
    {
      "s": 76.18,
      "e": 77.71,
      "text": "the Parker Solar Probe"
    },
    {
      "s": 77.78,
      "e": 79.34,
      "text": "which is a daring mission"
    },
    {
      "s": 79.41,
      "e": 81.25,
      "text": "to go into the very atmosphere,"
    },
    {
      "s": 81.31,
      "e": 82.52,
      "text": "the very heart"
    },
    {
      "s": 82.58,
      "e": 84.08,
      "text": "of the atmosphere of the sun."
    },
    {
      "s": 84.15,
      "e": 85.35,
      "text": "So I have a model"
    },
    {
      "s": 85.42,
      "e": 86.75,
      "text": "of the Parker Solar Probe"
    },
    {
      "s": 86.82,
      "e": 88.12,
      "text": "spacecraft here."
    },
    {
      "s": 88.19,
      "e": 88.82,
      "text": "Can I get some sun"
    },
    {
      "s": 88.89,
      "e": 90.72,
      "text": "in here, please?"
    },
    {
      "s": 90.79,
      "e": 91.96,
      "text": "So the important thing"
    },
    {
      "s": 92.03,
      "e": 93.39,
      "text": "is as the spacecraft"
    },
    {
      "s": 93.46,
      "e": 95.73,
      "text": "moves around the sun,"
    },
    {
      "s": 95.8,
      "e": 97.23,
      "text": "the heat shield has"
    },
    {
      "s": 97.3,
      "e": 99.1,
      "text": "to remain pointed towards"
    },
    {
      "s": 99.16,
      "e": 101.0,
      "text": "the sun at all times."
    },
    {
      "s": 101.07,
      "e": 102.03,
      "text": "So the heat shield--"
    },
    {
      "s": 102.1,
      "e": 103.2,
      "text": "the front of the heat shield"
    },
    {
      "s": 103.27,
      "e": 103.94,
      "text": "will get to about"
    },
    {
      "s": 104.0,
      "e": 106.71,
      "text": "2,500 degrees Fahrenheit."
    },
    {
      "s": 106.77,
      "e": 107.54,
      "text": "But the main body"
    },
    {
      "s": 107.61,
      "e": 109.11,
      "text": "of the spacecraft is nice"
    },
    {
      "s": 109.17,
      "e": 110.14,
      "text": "and cool at about"
    },
    {
      "s": 110.21,
      "e": 112.05,
      "text": "80 degrees Fahrenheit."
    },
    {
      "s": 112.11,
      "e": 113.71,
      "text": "Which is a bit like a balmy,"
    },
    {
      "s": 113.78,
      "e": 115.38,
      "text": "Florida evening in August"
    },
    {
      "s": 115.45,
      "e": 116.58,
      "text": "I guess!"
    },
    {
      "s": 116.65,
      "e": 118.72,
      "text": "And that's Parker Solar Probe."
    },
    {
      "s": 118.78,
      "e": 119.45,
      "text": "Thank you!"
    },
    {
      "s": 122.29,
      "e": 123.06,
      "text": "Good!"
    },
    {
      "s": 123.12,
      "e": 123.99,
      "text": "[ laughter ]"
    },
    {
      "s": 124.06,
      "e": 125.02,
      "text": ">> I love how polite you are!"
    },
    {
      "s": 125.09,
      "e": 126.69,
      "text": "[ laughter ]"
    },
    {
      "s": 126.76,
      "e": 127.66,
      "text": ">> So one of the things"
    },
    {
      "s": 127.73,
      "e": 128.5,
      "text": "that we discovered"
    },
    {
      "s": 128.56,
      "e": 129.63,
      "text": "with Parker Solar Probe"
    },
    {
      "s": 129.7,
      "e": 131.3,
      "text": "on the very first orbit"
    },
    {
      "s": 131.36,
      "e": 133.63,
      "text": "was switchbacks."
    },
    {
      "s": 133.7,
      "e": 134.77,
      "text": "Switchbacks..."
    },
    {
      "s": 134.83,
      "e": 135.7,
      "text": "If only I had a model"
    },
    {
      "s": 135.77,
      "e": 137.04,
      "text": "of The Corona."
    },
    {
      "s": 137.1,
      "e": 138.5,
      "text": "Oh, thank you!"
    },
    {
      "s": 138.57,
      "e": 140.11,
      "text": "So, switchbacks are really"
    },
    {
      "s": 140.17,
      "e": 142.84,
      "text": "reversals in the material"
    },
    {
      "s": 142.91,
      "e": 144.74,
      "text": "coming from the sun."
    },
    {
      "s": 144.81,
      "e": 146.98,
      "text": "So the sun has a magnetic field"
    },
    {
      "s": 147.05,
      "e": 148.18,
      "text": "and that is continually"
    },
    {
      "s": 148.25,
      "e": 149.12,
      "text": "moving away--"
    },
    {
      "s": 149.18,
      "e": 151.15,
      "text": "or so we thought, continually"
    },
    {
      "s": 151.22,
      "e": 152.75,
      "text": "moving away from the sun."
    },
    {
      "s": 152.82,
      "e": 153.45,
      "text": "But what we found"
    },
    {
      "s": 153.52,
      "e": 154.92,
      "text": "with Parker Solar Probe"
    },
    {
      "s": 154.99,
      "e": 156.02,
      "text": "is this magnetic field"
    },
    {
      "s": 156.09,
      "e": 156.76,
      "text": "actually kind of"
    },
    {
      "s": 156.82,
      "e": 158.16,
      "text": "reverses on itself"
    },
    {
      "s": 158.22,
      "e": 159.83,
      "text": "and makes an \"S\" shape."
    },
    {
      "s": 159.89,
      "e": 161.19,
      "text": "We call that a switchback."
    },
    {
      "s": 161.26,
      "e": 162.23,
      "text": "It's hard to twist"
    },
    {
      "s": 162.3,
      "e": 163.3,
      "text": "a magnetic field,"
    },
    {
      "s": 163.36,
      "e": 164.5,
      "text": "it's like trying to twist"
    },
    {
      "s": 164.56,
      "e": 166.73,
      "text": "a rubber hose-- it's hard!"
    },
    {
      "s": 166.8,
      "e": 168.07,
      "text": "And so, somehow there's"
    },
    {
      "s": 168.13,
      "e": 169.87,
      "text": "this energy going into th--"
    },
    {
      "s": 169.94,
      "e": 170.97,
      "text": "the magnetic field"
    },
    {
      "s": 171.04,
      "e": 172.7,
      "text": "that's causing this \"S\" shape."
    },
    {
      "s": 172.77,
      "e": 173.97,
      "text": "And when it releases,"
    },
    {
      "s": 174.04,
      "e": 175.47,
      "text": "it's letting all of this excess"
    },
    {
      "s": 175.54,
      "e": 179.01,
      "text": "energy out into the solar wind."
    },
    {
      "s": 179.08,
      "e": 180.35,
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "s": 180.41,
      "e": 181.95,
      "text": "Studying the sun is really"
    },
    {
      "s": 182.01,
      "e": 183.58,
      "text": "important as we get ready"
    },
    {
      "s": 183.65,
      "e": 185.52,
      "text": "to support the Artemis mission."
    },
    {
      "s": 185.59,
      "e": 186.52,
      "text": "We're really protected here"
    },
    {
      "s": 186.59,
      "e": 187.42,
      "text": "on the planet by our"
    },
    {
      "s": 187.49,
      "e": 188.85,
      "text": "magnetic field and all"
    },
    {
      "s": 188.92,
      "e": 190.69,
      "text": "of that atmosphere around us."
    },
    {
      "s": 190.76,
      "e": 192.49,
      "text": "Our astronauts, when they--"
    },
    {
      "s": 192.56,
      "e": 193.83,
      "text": "they will be on the moon."
    },
    {
      "s": 193.89,
      "e": 195.23,
      "text": "And of course, as we journey"
    },
    {
      "s": 195.29,
      "e": 197.63,
      "text": "further to Mars and beyond,"
    },
    {
      "s": 197.7,
      "e": 198.76,
      "text": "we'll be traveling through"
    },
    {
      "s": 198.83,
      "e": 200.5,
      "text": "the solar wind and living"
    },
    {
      "s": 200.57,
      "e": 202.1,
      "text": "really more in the atmosphere"
    },
    {
      "s": 202.17,
      "e": 203.5,
      "text": "of the sun."
    },
    {
      "s": 203.57,
      "e": 205.64,
      "text": "And so it's key as we"
    },
    {
      "s": 205.7,
      "e": 207.01,
      "text": "go forward to the moon,"
    },
    {
      "s": 207.07,
      "e": 208.01,
      "text": "to Mars and beyond"
    },
    {
      "s": 208.07,
      "e": 209.58,
      "text": "with our Artemis mission"
    },
    {
      "s": 209.64,
      "e": 210.88,
      "text": "that we really understand"
    },
    {
      "s": 210.94,
      "e": 212.08,
      "text": "the source of energy"
    },
    {
      "s": 212.15,
      "e": 212.68,
      "text": "in the heart"
    },
    {
      "s": 212.75,
      "e": 214.78,
      "text": "of our solar system."
    },
    {
      "s": 214.85,
      "e": 215.85,
      "text": "Parker Solar Probe"
    },
    {
      "s": 215.91,
      "e": 218.08,
      "text": "on her final closest approach"
    },
    {
      "s": 218.15,
      "e": 219.22,
      "text": "after she's done all"
    },
    {
      "s": 219.28,
      "e": 220.72,
      "text": "of those Venus flybys,"
    },
    {
      "s": 220.79,
      "e": 222.75,
      "text": "she will be about 3.9 million"
    },
    {
      "s": 222.82,
      "e": 225.12,
      "text": "miles above the sun's surface."
    },
    {
      "s": 225.19,
      "e": 225.93,
      "text": "We have many materials"
    },
    {
      "s": 225.99,
      "e": 227.19,
      "text": "on Parker Solar Probe"
    },
    {
      "s": 227.26,
      "e": 228.59,
      "text": "that don't melt despite"
    },
    {
      "s": 228.66,
      "e": 230.46,
      "text": "how close they are to the sun."
    },
    {
      "s": 230.53,
      "e": 231.4,
      "text": "In fact, that was one"
    },
    {
      "s": 231.46,
      "e": 232.5,
      "text": "of the big technology"
    },
    {
      "s": 232.56,
      "e": 234.23,
      "text": "challenges for us"
    },
    {
      "s": 234.3,
      "e": 235.63,
      "text": "to find materials not only"
    },
    {
      "s": 235.7,
      "e": 236.9,
      "text": "that don't melt,"
    },
    {
      "s": 236.97,
      "e": 238.14,
      "text": "but can actually withstand"
    },
    {
      "s": 238.2,
      "e": 239.17,
      "text": "the incredible change"
    },
    {
      "s": 239.24,
      "e": 240.41,
      "text": "in temperature because"
    },
    {
      "s": 240.47,
      "e": 241.67,
      "text": "Parker goes very close"
    },
    {
      "s": 241.74,
      "e": 243.81,
      "text": "to the sun and then comes out"
    },
    {
      "s": 243.88,
      "e": 245.48,
      "text": "around the orbit of Venus."
    },
    {
      "s": 245.54,
      "e": 246.58,
      "text": "Which means that all"
    },
    {
      "s": 246.65,
      "e": 247.65,
      "text": "these materials go really"
    },
    {
      "s": 247.71,
      "e": 249.68,
      "text": "hot and then really cold"
    },
    {
      "s": 249.75,
      "e": 252.69,
      "text": "at least 24 times."
    },
    {
      "s": 252.75,
      "e": 253.55,
      "text": "So the critical thing"
    },
    {
      "s": 253.62,
      "e": 254.42,
      "text": "for Parker Solar Probe,"
    },
    {
      "s": 254.49,
      "e": 255.25,
      "text": "of course, is to keep"
    },
    {
      "s": 255.32,
      "e": 256.25,
      "text": "that heat shield pointing"
    },
    {
      "s": 256.32,
      "e": 257.39,
      "text": "at the sun."
    },
    {
      "s": 257.46,
      "e": 258.52,
      "text": "At some point,"
    },
    {
      "s": 258.59,
      "e": 259.99,
      "text": "she will run out of fuel."
    },
    {
      "s": 260.06,
      "e": 261.53,
      "text": "At that point, unfortunately,"
    },
    {
      "s": 261.59,
      "e": 262.83,
      "text": "she will start to turn."
    },
    {
      "s": 262.89,
      "e": 264.13,
      "text": "And the full illumination"
    },
    {
      "s": 264.2,
      "e": 265.4,
      "text": "of the sun will hit parts"
    },
    {
      "s": 265.46,
      "e": 266.9,
      "text": "of the spacecraft that are not"
    },
    {
      "s": 266.97,
      "e": 268.9,
      "text": "designed to see the sun."
    },
    {
      "s": 268.97,
      "e": 269.67,
      "text": "And so she'll break up"
    },
    {
      "s": 269.74,
      "e": 270.94,
      "text": "into large pieces,"
    },
    {
      "s": 271.0,
      "e": 271.57,
      "text": "and then they will get"
    },
    {
      "s": 271.64,
      "e": 273.44,
      "text": "gradually smaller and smaller"
    },
    {
      "s": 273.51,
      "e": 275.24,
      "text": "until they become really tiny."
    },
    {
      "s": 275.31,
      "e": 275.94,
      "text": "And so I like to think"
    },
    {
      "s": 276.01,
      "e": 277.18,
      "text": "that she will become part"
    },
    {
      "s": 277.24,
      "e": 279.01,
      "text": "of the Corona, and she will"
    },
    {
      "s": 279.08,
      "e": 280.85,
      "text": "orbit the sun forever."
    },
    {
      "s": 280.91,
      "e": 282.08,
      "text": "So honestly, we don't know"
    },
    {
      "s": 282.15,
      "e": 282.85,
      "text": "what new science"
    },
    {
      "s": 282.92,
      "e": 284.02,
      "text": "we're going to expect."
    },
    {
      "s": 284.08,
      "e": 284.82,
      "text": "We've already seen"
    },
    {
      "s": 284.88,
      "e": 286.12,
      "text": "unbelievable stuff on"
    },
    {
